gsl3673: clear slot 0 on suspend and resume

The driver registers MAX_CONTACTS + 1 slots and reports contacts in slots
1..MAX_CONTACTS, yet the two sleep-time release loops started at 1, so a
contact parked in slot 0 survived every suspend (measured 2026-09-04: a
finger that never lifted froze glcube's resting spin). Release every
allocated slot, 0..MAX_CONTACTS.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/gsl3673.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/gsl3673.c
@@ -1040,7 +1040,7 @@
 #ifdef SLEEP_CLEAR_POINT
 	msleep(10);
 	#ifdef REPORT_DATA_ANDROID_4_0
-	for (i = 1; i <= MAX_CONTACTS; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i <= MAX_CONTACTS; i++) {
 		input_mt_slot(ts->input, i);
 		input_report_abs(ts->input, ABS_MT_TRACKING_ID, -1);
 		input_mt_report_slot_state(ts->input, MT_TOOL_FINGER, false);
@@ -1071,7 +1071,7 @@
 		return rc;
 #ifdef SLEEP_CLEAR_POINT
 	#ifdef REPORT_DATA_ANDROID_4_0
-	for (i = 1; i <= MAX_CONTACTS; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i <= MAX_CONTACTS; i++) {
 		input_mt_slot(ts->input, i);
 		input_report_abs(ts->input, ABS_MT_TRACKING_ID, -1);
 		input_mt_report_slot_state(ts->input, MT_TOOL_FINGER, false);
